<title>GERMANY: Prodi rebuffs suggestions Italy not at EMU launch.</title>
<headline>Prodi rebuffs suggestions Italy not at EMU launch.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian prime minister Romano Prodi rejected any suggestion that Italy may not be among the first nations to adopt a common European currency in 1999, saying that even a &quot;constructive delay&quot; would be unacceptable.</p>
<p>Asked whether a constructive delay, to give Italy more time to consolidate its finances, would be helpful, Prodi rebuffed the suggestion.</p>
<p>&quot;It is not a hypothesis which is in any way plausible. It does not even correspond to Chancellor Helmut Kohl's intentions as you have heard&quot;.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
